.PD
.PP
Personal preferences, such as another prefix or
.B |
and
.B \-
to split, belong in the configuration file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
set \-g prefix C\-a
bind C\-a send\-prefix
bind | split\-window \-h
bind \- split\-window \-v
bind h select\-pane \-L
.fi
.RE
.SH WINDOWS AND PANES
A window closes when its last pane exits and a session when its last window closes; clients of an
ended session are switched to another.
.PP
A window is named after the foreground program of its active pane, re-evaluated about twice a
second; renaming it with
.B ,
turns that off for the window.
The
.B ,
and
.B $
commands read the new name on the status line: Enter accepts, Escape cancels, C\-u clears.
An empty name, or a session name already in use, is refused.
.SH CHOOSING SESSIONS AND WINDOWS
The
.B s
and
.B w
commands display a list over the panes, with the entry the client currently shows marked by an
asterisk.
Keys do not reach the pane meanwhile.
.PP
.PD 0
.TP 20
.B Up, Down, k, j
Move the selection.
.TP
.B PageUp, PageDown
Move by ten entries.
.TP
.B Home, End, g, G
Select the first or last entry.
.TP
.B Enter
Switch to the selected session or window and close the list.
.TP
.B Escape, q
Close the list.
.PD
.SH COPY MODE
Copy mode shows a pane's scrollback with a cursor, using the vi or the emacs keys as
.B mode\-keys
says.
Enter it with the prefix and
.BR [ ,
or by scrolling the wheel up over a pane whose program uses neither the mouse nor the alternate
screen; scrolling back to the bottom then leaves it.
The top right shows
.RB [ lines\ from\ the\ bottom / lines\ of\ history ].
.PP
.BR copy\-mode " [" \-eHu "] [" \-t " \fIpane\fP]"
(also from a key: \fBbind PageUp copy\-mode \-u\fP) enters it for any pane, not only the active one,
and does not select that pane.
.B \-u
starts one page back,
.B \-e
leaves copy mode on scrolling back to the bottom, and
.B \-H
leaves out the position at the top right.
.PP
The vi keys:
.PP
.PD 0
.TP 20
.BR h\ j\ k\ l ,\ arrows
Move the cursor.
.TP
.BR 0\ ^\ $
Start of line, first non-blank, end of line.
.TP
.BR w\ b\ e ,\ W\ B\ E
Move by word, or by space-separated word.
.TP
.BR g ,\ G
Top and bottom of the history.
.TP
.BR H\ M\ L
Top, middle, and bottom of the view.
.TP
.BR C\-u\ C\-d ,\ C\-b\ C\-f
Scroll by half a screen or a screen; PageUp and PageDown scroll a screen.
.TP
.BR C\-y\ C\-e
Scroll by one line.
.TP
.BR /\ ? ,\ n\ N
Search forward or backward, and repeat.
A search with no capital letters ignores case; searches wrap around.
.TP
.BR v ,\ Space
Start or clear a selection.
.TP
.B V
Select whole lines.
.TP
.B C\-v
Switch between a selection of running text and a block of columns (a rectangle: the same columns
of every line, trailing blanks dropped); without a selection it starts a block.
.TP
.B o
Move the cursor to the other end of the selection.
.TP
.BR y ,\ Enter
Copy the selection and leave copy mode.
.TP
.B D
Copy from the cursor to the end of the line and leave.
.TP
.BR Escape ,\ q ,\ C\-c
Leave copy mode.
.PD
.PP
The emacs keys:
.PP
.PD 0
.TP 20
.BR C\-b\ C\-f\ C\-p\ C\-n ,\ arrows
Move the cursor.
.TP
.BR C\-a\ C\-e ,\ M\-m
